  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- BRD knowledge domain: the reserved `okf/_brd/` registry at the repository root holds one agent-authored bundle per Business Requirement Document. A registry-only root okf/ declares no component; a `_brd` inside any other bundle is a validation error.\n- Deterministic Word extraction: `brd ingest` and `brd extract` read a .docx with the BCL zip/XML readers only — headings, paragraphs, lists, and tables become an ordered section model with a whole-file digest; headers, footers, comments, and media are ignored. No new dependencies.\n- Comparison stays agent work: the tool never ranks or scores BRD similarity. Ingestion returns the outline, digest, and the existing BRD cards; the host agent judges duplicates, overlaps, extensions, and supersession, and authors index.md (typed relations) plus relations.md (the analysis).\n- Derived reverse relations: forward links in frontmatter are the only stored truth; supersededBy and friends are computed at read time, so ingesting a new BRD never edits a historical one.\n- Source drift: a BRD records its document's path and digest; changed bytes flag the bundle stale, an absent file only warns.\n- New MCP tools prepare_brd_ingest, read_brd_source, list_brds, and read_brd; validate_okf, check/pull, doctor, and `hook stop` cover BRD bundles; each `_brd/<slug>` is its own three-way sync unit.\n- BRD registers: a bundle now carries requirements.md, flows.md, dependencies.md, assumptions.md, risks.md, and backlog.md — typed elements with stable ids (REQ/FLW/DEP/ASM/CON/RSK/EPC/STY), the source section ids each was distilled from, and the full detail behind each under a heading named for its id. Validation covers the schema, referential integrity across registers, and the consequences of the agent's own judgments: a ready requirement needs acceptance criteria and an unblocked dependency, and a user story may only be written from a ready requirement.\n- New `analyze_brd` / `brd analyze`: source coverage with every section nobody recorded, the blocking closure that walks a missing dependency to the flows it stops end to end, the assumptions, constraints, and risks the document never declares, everything too vague for a user story with its gaps, and backlog coverage — all derived, never inferred.\n- New `read_brd_history` / `brd history`: a bundle's revisions, the element-level difference between two of them with each field's old and new value, and any document's exact text at a revision so a change can be reverted by an authored write.\n- Mermaid diagrams are the one carve-out in the no-code profile, permitted inside BRD bundles only and checked to be real diagrams, so business flows and user journeys can carry their flowcharts.\n- Agent integration: init generates three Claude Code subagents, one per pass — octoevidence-brd-analyst records the document in full, octoevidence-brd-gap-analyst finds what it never says, octoevidence-brd-backlog plans from what it settled — and the authoring guide gains a `brd-analysis` section carrying the method.",
